direction: down
"capture": "capture\nReserve native task and trace schema before wrapper\ninvalidation/free; per-wrapper release right, not\npointer identity"
"derived-credit": "derived-credit\nAccepted parent owns reserved child credit before\npublication; unknown publication cannot be replayed"
"device-cursor": "device-cursor\nDetach, RD, WR and final release are distinct\nresumable phases; partial failure retains exact\ncursor"
"owner": "owner\nPSTATE FDSET use is not arbitrary worker execution;\nold roster and wake-to-sync-op service remain\navailable"
"release-outcome": "release-outcome\nFinal release may free native self despite error; no\nraw-pointer retry based on status alone"
"storage-commit": "storage-commit\nAt a safe epoch publish canonical RC/still owner,\nroot adapter and capacity ledger together; lost\nreply leaves target owning"
"accounting": "accounting\nRC bytes and still physical words/deferred quota are\nseparate; no double census at transfer"
"vm-permit": "vm-permit\nExternal ingress closed, child credit zero,\noutcomes/roots/readers drained, affinity and\nservices settled before any facility teardown"
"capture" -> "derived-credit": "Child custody requires captured\nparent right"
"capture" -> "device-cursor": "Cursor must own native lifetime"
"owner" -> "device-cursor": "Wait resume requires attached\nexecution owner"
"release-outcome" -> "device-cursor": "Cursor result must distinguish\nnative consumption"
"capture" -> "storage-commit": "Transfer requires rooted\ncaptured payload"
"accounting" -> "storage-commit": "Scan and census authority commit\ntogether"
"derived-credit" -> "vm-permit": "No accepted or reserved\ndescendant debt"
"owner" -> "vm-permit": "Old roster and thread affinity\nsettled"
"release-outcome" -> "vm-permit": "No unresolved external residue"
"storage-commit" -> "vm-permit": "Canonical storage acknowledged\nbefore teardown"
proof: "SysML -> ASCENT -> QNT / Lean; source + platform OPEN"
"vm-permit" -> proof
gain0: "collector\nB callback waiting time may leave collective critical\npath; no bounded latency unless admitted profiles\nterminate"
proof -> gain0
gain1: "storage\nFor H moved domains, 0 uncovered domains and exactly H\ncanonical scan/census entries; not a speed measurement"
proof -> gain1
gain2: "closure\nSaved duplicate work exceeds capture, dispatch,\nbarriers and retention cost; arbitrary hooks may remain\ninline or rejected"
proof -> gain2
gain3: "language\nZig does not remove root, effect, affinity, reclamation\nor termination proofs; no demonstrated incremental\nlanguage benefit"
proof -> gain3
